  "title": "Samnite House",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/townhouse"
  ],
  "details": "<p>The Samnite House originally occupied the entirety of the southern part of Insula V and included a three-sided peristyle. The plot was subdivided in the first century A.D. The house is noted for its well-preserved atrium\u00a0that still stands to two stories (three sides\u00a0with pilasters and interspersed latticed fences and one side with a loggia).</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The so-called \"Samnite House\" is a domus in Herculaneum that originally dates to the second century B.C., making it one of the oldest buildings discovered at the site.",
